# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the two values.
# .env.local matches *.local in .gitignore and never reaches the repository.
#
# Where to find them (checked against the dashboard on 2026-11-02):
#   Supabase dashboard -> the "Connect" button at the top -> Framework
#   The .env.local tab there shows both values.
#
# The dashboard prints them as NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY. This is Vite, not Next.js, so the
# names below are what the app reads — only the prefix differs, the values
# are the same. Vite exposes a variable to the browser only if its name
# starts with VITE_.
#
# The key is the publishable one (it starts with sb_publishable_). It is meant
# to ship inside the browser; what keeps the data private is row level
# security on the tables, not this key being secret (判断の記録 #57).
#
# The same two values also go into Vercel, under
#   Project Settings -> Environment Variables
# and a redeploy is needed afterwards: the values are baked in at build time,
# so adding them changes nothing until the next build.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
